---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '~/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Callout from '~/components/Callout.astro';
import { breadcrumbList } from '~/utils/jsonld';
import { SITE } from '~/data/site';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { name: 'Security', href: '/security' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Security"
  description="How PesaTrack protects your data — threat model, storage, permissions, and what we can't protect you from."
  canonical="/security"
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbList(crumbs)]}
  prose
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />

  <h1>Security</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Individual transaction records stay on the device. When you choose to use
    Pro AI, the app sends an anonymised spending digest and, for chat, your
    question and recent turns. Chat history is stored locally, analytics are
    off by default, and the app can be locked with a PIN.
  </p>

  <h2>What we protect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Confidentiality of transaction records.</strong> Your raw
      transaction rows, recipient names, budgets, and notes live in a private
      Room database inside the app's sandbox. Other apps on your phone can't
      read it. Pro AI requests don't send raw SMS or individual transaction
      rows; Ask Your Money sends your question and recent turns with an
      anonymised aggregate digest. See
      <a href="/privacy#ask-your-money">Privacy §5.9</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Local chat storage.</strong> Ask Your Money conversations are
      stored on-device to support resuming after restart. Clear them from the
      chat menu; database backups may include them. Device encryption and the
      app's sandbox are the protection boundary.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics are opt-in and anonymous.</strong> The app does
      hold <code>INTERNET</code> for <em>opt-in</em> Firebase Analytics.
      Off by default. When on, we never send SMS content, transaction
      amounts, recipient names, category names, or note text.
      See <a href="/privacy#analytics">Privacy § Analytics</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Casual access.</strong> The optional PIN lock plus biometric
      unlock stops someone who picks up your unlocked phone from browsing
      your finances.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we cannot protect against</h2>
  <Callout variant="warning" title="Be honest about threat model">
    <p>
      PesaTrack's PIN is designed to defeat <em>casual</em> access. It is not a
      substitute for a strong device passcode. A determined attacker with
      forensic tools and physical access to an unlocked device can, in
      principle, read the app's database.
    </p>
    <p>
      If your threat model includes that scenario, keep Android's disk
      encryption on (it is by default on modern devices), use a strong device
      passcode, and don't enable "remember device" on biometric.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Permissions we ask for</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>READ_SMS</code> / <code>RECEIVE_SMS</code> — to auto-detect M-PESA
      and NCBA transactions. See <a href="/faq#does-pesatrack-read-all-sms">the FAQ</a>
      for what we do and don't read.</li>
    <li><code>POST_NOTIFICATIONS</code> — for the "new transaction" and
      "uncategorised" notifications. Optional.</li>
    <li><code>USE_BIOMETRIC</code> — only if you enable biometric unlock.</li>
    <li><code>SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM</code> — for recurring reminders you set.</li>
    <li><code>INTERNET</code> / <code>ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE</code> — for opt-in
      Firebase Analytics and Pro AI calls when you use Coach Insights or Ask
      Your Money. AI requests carry aggregated/anonymised financial data and
      the text you choose to submit; see <a href="/privacy#data-sharing">Privacy §5</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we deliberately don't ask for</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>READ_CONTACTS.</strong> We resolve recipients from the SMS
      itself, not from your address book.</li>
    <li><strong>Location.</strong> We do not want it.</li>
    <li><strong>Ad SDKs, cross-app IDs, third-party trackers.</strong> None.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reporting a security issue</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> with
    "SECURITY" in the subject line. Please do not open a public GitHub issue
    for a vulnerability that could be exploited before a fix ships.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
